From 96683eae5f1a549904474a763be914c981dbce19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:21:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Dashboard: per-location status, delete messages, remove the
 double-up
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Store status is now one tile PER location — each shows its own Open / Closed
  or event countdown (Mitchell, Tulip Tops, Press Club…), instead of a single
  ambiguous 'Closed'. Tiles flow to any number of locations.
- Removed the duplicated 'Upcoming reservations' and 'New messages' stat tiles;
  the counts now live in their detail-card headers, so the number and the list
  aren't shown twice.
- Messages can be deleted (dashboard + Store → Customer messages): new
  /api/admin/messages/delete + db.deleteMessage.
- Upcoming closures card spans full width, removing the empty cell/gap beside it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0187Jj4Q77V4UPawzEh9gsGr
